# Snapshot of the shellcheck findings that already existed when the lint gate
# was introduced (SI-80). `just lint` fails when the count goes *up*, so new
# code is held to a clean bar without this phase silently absorbing the
# cleanup that belongs to SI-81 and SI-82.
#
# Started at 20. SI-81 took it to 14, not as a cleanup pass but as a side
# effect: the pre-commit hook requires *staged* files to be clean rather than
# merely at baseline, so every file that phase touched had to lose its existing
# findings too. The rest is SI-82's.
#
# SI-82 took it to 9, the same way — every bin/ script it routed through
# bin/lib/ had to be clean to get past the hook. What it cleared:
#   claude-backup      SC2012  `ls -t | head -5` -> find -exec stat | sort -rn
#   homebrew-restore   SC2046  unquoted $(hostname), twice  -> host_id
#   screenshot         SC2048  unquoted $* -> "$@"
#                      SC2086  same line
#
# SI-84 took it to 4, by deleting the files rather than by fixing them. The
# hand-written `aliases` and `session-variables.sh` are now generated from
# shell/*.spec, and the generator does not emit any of what they were flagged
# for. What it cleared:
#   aliases              SC2139 x3  double-quoted bodies, so $HOME expanded at
#                                   definition -> single-quoted now
#                        SC2142     `alias ia='open $1 …'`; aliases cannot take
#                                   positional parameters, and `open -a APP
#                                   FILE` never needed one
#   session-variables.sh SC2155     export X=$(cmd) -> assign, then export
#
# The generated files themselves add zero findings, which is the bar they have
# to keep: they are in shell_sources, so shfmt and shellcheck both see them.
#
# The 4 that remain belong to SI-84's follow-up (the functions consolidation,
# phase 5d) and to bash_profile:
#   bash_profile         SC1090 x2
#   functions/fcd.sh     SC2164
#   functions/fco.sh     SC2016
#
# Hand-edited rather than regenerated: `just lint-snapshot` rewrites this file
# from a heredoc in bin/dotfiles-lint and would destroy every comment above.
shellcheck=4
